cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  cooling_stack: a modular 1D cooling-stack design tool for small
  gas-turbine combustor liners
authors:
  - family-names: Yang
    given-names: Yang
    email: yybelinda@gmail.com
    website: https://github.com/yybelinda
version: 1.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-21"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yybelinda/cooling_stack"
abstract: >-
  A serial-path, single-node cooling-stack model for the liner of small
  gas-turbine combustors. Cold-side modules (smooth backside convection,
  ribbed channel, impingement) and hot-side film rows are composed freely
  along the coolant path; the solver closes the energy balance on the
  cold-side wall temperature by bisection, including coolant heat-up and
  a pressure-drop budget. Includes an automatic advice layer that flags
  wall-temperature margin, cold-side saturation, and film-ineffectiveness
  conditions.
keywords:
  - combustor cooling
  - film cooling
  - impingement cooling
  - 1D design
  - gas turbine
